The cpp-bestpractices port provides composable INTERFACE targets for compiler
warnings, standard library hardening, and sanitizers.

Available targets:
    cpp-bestpractices::lite              - Baseline warnings & compiler hygiene
    cpp-bestpractices::cpp-bestpractices - Recommended strict warnings (includes lite)
    cpp-bestpractices::paranoid          - Extra-strict warnings (includes default)
    cpp-bestpractices::werror            - Treat warnings as errors (-Werror / /WX)
    cpp-bestpractices::hardening         - STL bounds/precondition assertions
    cpp-bestpractices::asan              - Address & Undefined Behavior Sanitizers
    cpp-bestpractices::tsan              - Thread Sanitizer

Example usage in CMakeLists.txt:

    find_package(cpp-bestpractices CONFIG REQUIRED)

    target_link_libraries(my-target PRIVATE
        cpp-bestpractices::cpp-bestpractices
        cpp-bestpractices::hardening
        $<$<BOOL:${WARNINGS_AS_ERRORS}>:cpp-bestpractices::werror>
        $<$<BOOL:${ENABLE_SANITIZERS}>:cpp-bestpractices::asan>
    )

    cpp_bestpractices_add_format_targets(my-target my-tests)

Optional vcpkg feature:
    Enable "features": ["skills"] in vcpkg.json to install the AI agent skill
    and automatically register vcpkg agent skills into .agents/skills.json.
